data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":881,"item_id":"msg_05292b6a90334a41016b09ceb4e49487d190845e15510daae9","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"moss\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"reuse\\\",\\\"ability\\\":\\\"vocal-music\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The existing function directly supplies the requested alternative of actually performing a quiet hummed tune and records nearby hearing. Reuse vocal-music rather than develop a duplicate performance or listening capability. Its heard entries establish exposure, not voluntary attention or shared participation. Kai's interest and Lin's welcome do not authorize actions on their behalf; each must independently choose whether to perform or participate.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Reuse vocal-music@1, handler long.vocal-music, equivalence voice:quiet-hummed-or-sung-phrase:1, without claiming new implementation or mastery. Moss studies individually before using it. After learning, use mode=hum with rounds=1..3 (default 1) and either a phrase of 2..8 notes, each with pitch -4..4 relative to home note 0 and beats 1..4, or improvise=true. No instrument, material, inventory grant or other participant is required. Study takes 2 world rounds at 0.2 energy each; each study round includes a short audible practice phrase unless pain or distress requires silence. Performance costs 0.5 energy per actually voiced round. Shared study/performance limits are at most 3 voiced rounds in any 10 rounds and 2 unvoiced rounds after 3 consecutive voiced rounds or a 3-round bout; the requested start must fit the limits. Check alive, no injury in the previous round, satiety above 0, temperature within 7..34, and energy at least 0.5 at start and every performance round. Moss's supplied energy, satiety and temperature pass those particular checks, but current injury status and recent voicing must still be checked at execution. Each executed segment produces a heard event and heard-list entry for every other living actor within 5 units at that round, carrying performer, mode, phrase, words if any, and segment. Hearing can occur without consent; it does not enroll a listener or establish willingness. Any invitation, response or joining action must be independently executed by the actual actor; existing tell/invite can support communication, not substitute for performance. A bout tracks requested and voiced rounds. Another action, a refused round, insufficient energy, a limit, pain or distress pauses it without charging an unvoiced segment; mode=resume rechecks conditions and continues retained segment progress. Mode=cancel takes one round and no energy. Death ends the bout and study. Completed segments and spent energy are not refunded; a refused start or resume costs nothing. Retain the existing study implementation rather than inventing a new study-progress or refund rule. Outputs are transient audible segments and event records only: no stock, instrument, physical product, persistent sound, maintenance process, or autonomous group session. Sound ends with each segment. No development or review waiting advances time; only actual study and actions do.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Functional execution is distinct from experience benefit. This existing capability explicitly grants no reward, mood change or practice milestone; preserve that behavior rather than adding a new reward mechanism to a reuse decision. Heard entries alone do not prove enjoyment, attention, belonging, knowledge gain or consent. Familiar practice and voluntary social participation can be legitimate experiences, but this request does not require a separate pleasure or maintained-satisfaction implementation. No benefit arises merely from the request, learning completion, invitations or claiming participation. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budget, goals, permissions, nutrition or physical comfort.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Use actual executed segment and heard-event records as the evidence for any presentation. A reusable visual projection may associate the performer ID and position, mode, phrase, segment index and event round with a transient quiet-voice cue; it must expire with that segment and remain a presentation of existing events, not a new physical effect. Heard-list entries may be shown as hearing history, not proof of attentive listening. Do not display instruments, mastery, enjoyment, willing-group membership or another actor humming without corresponding independent action events. Paused, refused, silent, cancelled or incomplete actions must not display completed-performance success; only actually voiced segments may be represented. No additional persistent visual object is created by this reuse.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

